# The pins of scope_surface.rs (HT-SURF, §5.2 Q-LEXSCOPE LS1 part 4, DELTA10 L1 / L2), one
# section per table: a line `== NAME` opens it ; `#` lines are notes ; a table is tab-separated,
# its first line a header ; a COUNTS / PRESENT section is one line compared verbatim.
# SURF_* = the real crate's (`crate::lexscope`) ; FIX_* = the fixture modules'
# (scope_surface.fixtures). SURF_VOCAB / SURF_TRAITS are the vocabulary both use. LS1 part 5
# (DELTA11 R2) adds the counted lists CARD, CB, BODY and the hash column of MACROS, each with
# its FIX_ twin ; LS1 part 6 adds INTERIOR's exemptions (SURF_INTERIOR, empty, and FIX_INTERIOR) ;
# with the module absent every SURF_ list is empty (a row is STALE).
== SURF_VOCAB
# HT's table of opaque lexscope types: plan10/g/surface.tsv's 12 TYPE rows (DELTA10 L1 I-SURF's
# list: ScopeRef, Saved, the witness = ScopeWitness (DELTA9's name, not yet checked by names.py),
# Shown, ShownCtx, ScopeKeyed<V>, SavedChain, SavedRoot, SavedMethod, ReportedAt ; Scopes (the
# tier-K receiver) ; Mark, the mark selector, an enum: also on ENUMS when it exists) + DK1's
# NewKey, AtKey, DeclKey, Keyed<V>. A name here passes only where the file set DEFINES it as
# the kind written.
name	kind
Scopes	struct
Saved	struct
ScopeWitness	struct
Shown	struct
ShownCtx	struct
SavedChain	struct
SavedRoot	struct
SavedMethod	struct
ScopeRef	struct
ScopeKeyed	struct
Mark	enum
ReportedAt	struct
NewKey	struct
AtKey	struct
DeclKey	struct
Keyed	struct
== SURF_TRAITS
# the crate-visible traits allowed (plan10/g/surface.tsv: 1, the boundary trait)
name
Outgoing
== SURF_MACROS
# MACRO-BODY (DELTA11 R2): every `macro_rules!` the file set defines, or the rest of the crate
# defines and the file set calls, with the sha256 of its token tree ; also the item-position
# macros allowed. Empty until the module exists (a row with no definition is STALE): `zn`'s row
# and hash come with LS2a (DELTA11 R6), read by its delta judge (NP-5).
name	sha256
== SURF_PRESENT
absent
== SURF_COUNTS
present=absent files=0 rows=0 out_types=0 e_fns=0 text_flows=0
== SURF_ROWS
# the computed surface: one row per OUT position / IN text parameter / type / impl / use
file	tier	kind	item	position	type	verdict
== SURF_OUT_TYPES
# SURF_OUT_TYPES, the closed list J1 asked for: the distinct normalised OUT types
type
== SURF_LEAVE
# LEAVE: text out, counted, each with its closing unit (DELTA10 L1: L0 BOUNDARY, L1-L5) — empty
# until the module exists ; a row matching no failing position fails STALE
id	item	position	type	closes
== SURF_ENTER
# ENTER: text in, by role (to-scope / to-display / lookup)
item	param	role
== SURF_ENUMS
# crate-visible enums allowed (payload-free): the mark selector at LS3
name
== SURF_SHIMS
# RT-a shims (DELTA10 L2): shim, the private fn it wraps, the wrapper
shim	private	wrapper
== SURF_OUTGOING
# the boundary's impls (pinned 2 from LS2-d: Shown -> String, ShownCtx -> Vec<diag::Frame>)
type	plain
== SURF_E
# E: the Elaborator-taking fns, OUT-F / OUT-C / OUT-M by (fn, name, count) ; FLOW (hand) in /
# payload / text:<sink> (BODY moved to SURF_BODY: BODY-ALL, DELTA11 R2)
item	kind	name	count	flow
== SURF_CARD
# CARD (DELTA11 R2): an OUT position holding Option / Vec / a slice / an array / two or more
# `bool`, with MEANS (hand): caller | hit:<question> | list:<what> ; a missing row FAILS CARD,
# a row matching no position is STALE. First rows at LS2a.
item	position	type	means
== SURF_CB
# CB (DELTA11 R2): a callback parameter of a surface item, kind Fn | FnMut | FnOnce | fn, its
# argument types, CALLS (hand): once (FnOnce) | per:<what> | probe:<what>. First rows at LS2a.
item	param	kind	args	calls
== SURF_BODY
# BODY-ALL (DELTA11 R2, R4 N-5): the sha256 of the body tokens of every fn of the file set.
# First rows at LS2a ; each unit's verify prints the rows that changed.
file	fn	sha256
== SURF_INTERIOR
# INTERIOR (LS1 part 6): the exemptions, each a counted, named row (as LEAVE / ENTER are):
# item, position, the path of names INTERIOR follows to the carrier, why (hand). A row whose
# path moved FAILS INTERIOR ; a row matching no position is STALE. Empty.
item	position	reaches	why
== SURF_PLAN
# SURF-PLAN: the 30 fns of plan10/g/moved.tsv (DELTA10 L2), judged by I-SURF on today's signature
# (vis, tier, the normalised signature, verdict, the failing positions, the text IN parameters) ;
# + report_at (L2's LS3 row, N-a), which moved.tsv does not list: 31 rows. LS1 part 5 (DELTA11
# R2): CARD and CB judge them too, with no list consulted (as LEAVE is not): 16 CARD, 8 CB.
# LS1 part 6: INTERIOR judges them too, no list consulted: 1 row (with_scope's callback lends
# `&mut Self`, the Elaborator, which holds a RefCell: lib.rs:555 const_call_fn).
